| `apps/desktop`      | Tauri shell; the API becomes a single `.exe` via `bun build --compile` |

Patterns borrowed from the proven `tuari_react_hono` ERP monorepo in `D:\projects`.

## Run (dev)

```bash
bun install
bun run dev:api        # API on http://127.0.0.1:4317
bun run dev:web        # UI on http://localhost:5173
bun run dev:desktop    # Tauri window (needs Rust toolchain. installed)
```

Production distribution: `bun run --filter @dokan/api compile` → `dokan-api` binary, shipped as the Tauri sidecar; web builds to static files the Tauri webview serves.

Decisions are recorded in `docs/adr/`. Domain terms in `CONTEXT.md`.===SMOKE main check===
import { Database } from "bun:sqlite";
import { serve } from "@hono/node-server";
import { Hono } from "hono";

import { createAppConfig } from "./config";
import { AppLogger, localDateTime } from "./lib/logger";

/** Tiny skeleton boot — proves the stack works end-to-end before real code lands. */
const config = createAppConfig();
const logger = new AppLogger(config.dataDir);

// SQLite proof: a table is created, written, and read back.
const sqlite = new Database(`${config.dataDir}/dokan.db`, { create: true });
sqlite.exec("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS smoke (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, note TEXT)");
sqlite.query("INSERT INTO smoke (note) VALUES (?)").run("hello from bun:sqlite");
// SAFETY: the smoke table's note column is TEXT; the insert above guarantees a row
const row = sqlite.query("SELECT note FROM smoke ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1").get() as { note: string };

const app = new Hono();

app.get("/health", (c) =>
  c.json({
    ok: true,
    version: config.version,
    db: row.note,
    time: localDateTime(),
  }),
);

